      "latency_ms": 36651.5,
      "prompt_tokens": 18,
      "completion_tokens": 1159,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**, which means it is made up of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what that actually means and why water is so special:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\n*   **Oxygen:** This is a heavy, highly reactive element that usually grabs electrons from other atoms.\n*   **Hydrogen:** This is a light, non-reactive element.\n*   **The Bond:** When these atoms come together, the oxygen atom pulls the hydrogen atoms close to it. This creates a \"V\" shape. Because the oxygen end of the molecule is slightly negative and the hydrogen ends are slightly positive, water is a **polar molecule**.\n\n### 2. States of Matter\nWater is unique because it can exist in all three states of matter at or near the temperature of the human body:\n*   **Solid (Ice):** When frozen, the molecules move slowly and lock into a rigid crystal lattice.\n*   **Liquid:** At room temperature, the molecules move freely but stay close together, allowing water to flow and take the shape of its container.\n*   **Gas (Steam/Vapor):** When heated, the molecules move so fast that they break free from one another and fill the air.\n\n### 3. Unique Properties\nBecause of its chemical structure, water has several properties that make it essential for life:\n*   **The Universal Solvent:** Water is excellent at dissolving other substances. This is why it is the main transport system in plants and animals (blood is mostly water).\n*   **High Surface Tension:** Water molecules stick to each other very strongly. This allows small insects to walk across the surface of a puddle without sinking.\n*   **High Specific Heat:** Water can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot itself. This helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps the human body from overheating.\n\n### 4. Importance on Earth\nWater covers about 71% of the Earth's surface. It is the only substance found naturally on Earth in all three states, and it is the only known planet in our solar system to have liquid water on its surface. All known forms of life require water to survive."
